meta {
  name: Get Space Credential (space.getSpaceCredential)
  type: http
  seq: 141
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/xrpc/com.atproto.space.getSpaceCredential
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Signature-Input: atproto-space=("authorization");keyid="{{spaceKeyId}}"
  Signature: atproto-space=:{{spaceSignature}}:
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{delegationToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "space": "at://did:plc:exampleauthority/space/org.example.bucket/self",
    "clientAttestation": "{{clientAttestation}}"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://localhost:8080
  delegationToken: <token from getDelegationToken on the user's PDS>
  spaceKeyId: <the client's P-256 did:key (did:key:zDn…) — becomes the credential's cnf.kid>
  spaceSignature: <base64 raw r||s ECDSA-P256-SHA256 signature by that key over the RFC 9421 base: '"authorization": Bearer {{delegationToken}}' LF '"@signature-params": ("authorization");keyid="{{spaceKeyId}}"'>
  clientAttestation: <ES256 atproto-client-attestation+jwt signed by a key in the client's metadata JWKS: iss = sub = client_id, aud {authorityDid}#atproto_space_host, fresh iat/exp, single-use jti — omit the field entirely for a space with #open app access>
}

docs {
  Atproto Spaces (proposal 0016). Called on the space authority's PDS: exchanges the delegation
  token (the request's Authorization token) plus an RFC 9421 `atproto-space` signature over
  that header for a 10 min space credential (`typ atproto-space-credential+jwt`, `kid
  #atproto_space`, no `aud`, `cnf.kid` = the signature's did:key). The credential is then
  presented as `Authorization: Atproto-Space <credential>` with an `Atproto-Space-Audience`
  header (the repo owner's DID on a repo read, the authority's on a space-level one) and a
  signature covering both, by the `cnf.kid` key.

  `clientAttestation` is required only for a space whose appAccess is `#allowList`, and is
  verified whenever present: `client_id` (its `iss`/`sub`) is resolved to its client-metadata
  document and the JWKS that document publishes, and the `jti` is spent single-use. The
  attested client_id is what the allow list is matched against, and what is forwarded to a
  managing app's checkUserAccess.

  Errors (lexicon names): SpaceNotFound (unknown, or not anchored on an account here),
  SpaceDeleted, InvalidDelegationToken (bad signature/typ/kid/sub/aud/exp, or already used —
  the token is single-use), InvalidClientAttestation (malformed, unresolvable client_id, wrong
  signature/aud, expired, or replayed), UserNotAuthorized (refused on the requesting user:
  member-list non-member, or a managing app that answered no / could not be reached),
  AppNotAuthorized (refused on the requesting app: no attestation, or an attested client_id
  that is not on the space's allow list).
}
